# OpenHands Swarm

Well-structured Python implementation of the OpenHands issue orchestration model, including:

- Phase/state machine policy
- Transition guards
- `lock`-based lease semantics
- In-memory issue orchestration service
- CLI for validation and transition simulation
- Unit tests for invariants and transitions

## Project layout

```text
src/openhands_swarm/
  __init__.py
  cli.py
  config.py
  domain.py
  policy.py
  service.py
tests/
  test_policy.py
  test_service.py
state-machine-policy-and-workflow-descriptions.md
```

## Install

```bash
python -m pip install -e .[dev]
```

## Run tests

```bash
pytest
```

## CLI examples

Validate issue labels:

```bash
openhands-swarm validate --phase-labels phase:queen --meta-labels lock
```

Simulate transition:

```bash
openhands-swarm transition --phase phase:queen --open-questions false
```

Acquire and release lock in simulation:

```bash
openhands-swarm lock --owner run-123
openhands-swarm unlock --owner run-123
```
